{
  "id": "com.usuario.soul",
  "name": "Proyect Zelda's Soul",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "author": "ScrappySkyler",
  "description": "Proyect Zelda's soul turns Twilight Princess combat into a Sekiro-style posture duel. Tap R just before an enemy strike lands to parry it, break their posture, and punish them with a clean finisher combo. It works in both directions: enemies can parry you back, and your own posture bar fills if you play carelessly.SUPPORTED ENEMIES: Chilfos, Darknuts, Bokoblins, Lizalfos, Stalfos and Bulblins. All other enemies keep vanilla behavior.\n\nPARRYING\n- Tap R to open a short parry window (5 ticks). Time it with the enemy's strike.\n- A successful parry plays the Midna jump sound, a camera shake and a shield-bash animation. Link stays planted, with no step forward.\n- A parry is never a free hit: the enemy keeps attacking, so timing matters.\n- Auto-shield on lock-on is disabled. Blocking is always your choice.\n\nENEMY POSTURE BAR\n- A white bar appears over the locked-on enemy and fills with each parry.\n- Parries needed: Chilfos, Bokoblin and Bulblin: 1. Darknut, Lizalfos and Stalfos: 2.\n- The bar slowly drains over time (1.5% per second).\n- When full, the enemy is stunned, the bar glows, and you get a window to punish.\n\nFINISHER COMBO (full enemy bar)\n- Press B for a Mortal Draw, or press A for a Helm Splitter.\n- Once the first attack finishes, press B for a spinning slash, or A for another Helm Splitter.\n- Attacks never overlap: mash the buttons and Link still performs each one cleanly.\n- After a normal parry that does not fill the bar, one B press performs a single Mortal Draw. After that, attacks are normal.\n- Stunned enemies cannot parry you.\n\nENEMIES FIGHT BACK\n- Enemies attack 25% faster, wait less between strikes and are harder to flinch.\n- Enemies can parry your sword strikes (50% chance), which pushes Link back. They do not parry while stunned.\n- When an enemy parries you, its own posture bar drops by 15%.\n\nLINK'S POSTURE BAR\n- A bar at the bottom of the screen appears while you are locked on to any lockable enemy.\n- Normally blocking a hit adds 25%. An enemy parrying your sword adds 50%.\n- Each of your successful parries restores 25%. The bar also drains by 2% per second.\n- When it fills, Link is stunned for 3 seconds with a death-style collapse animation, a golden glow and a sound cue. The bar then empties in a quarter of a second.\n\nSHIELD BASH\n- Enemies on the parry list: no shield bash. R is your parry button.\n- All other enemies: double-tap R for the vanilla shield bash.\n\nCredits:Based on the lazy tweak mod, download that mod if you want more content."
}
